---
import { PRICE, REPO_URL, SHIPPED } from "../config";
import Logo from "./Logo.astro";
---

<section
  id="cta"
  class="relative flex flex-col items-center gap-5 overflow-hidden border-t border-rule px-0 pt-26 pb-23 text-center"
>
  <div
    class="glow pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 -bottom-[260px] h-[540px]"
    style="background:radial-gradient(42% 58% at 50% 100%,rgb(242 137 92 / 26%),transparent 70%)"
    aria-hidden="true"
  >
  </div>

  <Logo size={76} class="float relative shadow-[0_22px_44px_-18px_rgb(242_137_92/60%)]" />

  <h2
    class="relative m-0 max-w-[19ch] font-display text-[clamp(32px,5.4vw,50px)] leading-[1.06] font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-balance"
  >
    One process. One grant of trust. Read the source.
  </h2>

  <p class="relative m-0 max-w-[52ch] px-5 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.6] text-fg/56 text-pretty">
    A program that holds every credential you own should be readable and compilable by the people
    trusting it. The source is public and stays public; what is sold is the signed build.
  </p>

  {/*
    `SHIPPED` gates the elements that name something you can get. Everything else
    on this page is true whether or not there is a release, which is the rule
    config.ts states: a string outside a SHIPPED branch has to stand on its own.

    Buy points at /buy rather than at Stripe. That path is a redirect the site
    owns, so the checkout URL can move without editing a page — and the app's
    Licence pane links the same one, which matters more, because a URL compiled
    into a shipped binary can never be repointed.
  */}
  <div class="relative flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3 px-5 pt-1.5">
    {
      SHIPPED && (
        <a
          href="/download"
          class="plate rounded-md px-6 py-3.5 text-[15px] font-semibold text-accent-ink shadow-[0_14px_34px_-14px_rgb(242_137_92/75%)]"
        >
          Download for macOS
        </a>
      )
    }
    <a
      href={REPO_URL}
      rel="noopener"
      class:list={[
        "rounded-md px-6 py-3.5 text-[15px] font-semibold",
        SHIPPED
          ? "border border-white/10 bg-white/5 text-fg/80"
          : "plate text-accent-ink shadow-[0_14px_34px_-14px_rgb(242_137_92/75%)]",
      ]}
    >
      Read the source ↗
    </a>
    <code
      class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/5 px-4.5 py-3.5 font-mono text-[13px] text-fg/72"
    >
      make app && make audit
    </code>
  </div>

  {
    SHIPPED ? (
      <p class="relative m-0 text-[12.5px] text-fg/38">
        {PRICE.amount} — {PRICE.covers}. {PRICE.refund}.{" "}
        <a href="/buy" class="text-accent-hi underline underline-offset-2">
          Buy a licence
        </a>{" "}
        ·{" "}
        <a href="/terms" class="underline underline-offset-2">
          terms
        </a>
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p class="relative m-0 text-[12.5px] text-fg/38">
        {/* The unreachable half of the flag today, and it still has to be true:
            it said the app was code-signed for development only, which stopped
            being the case at 1.0.0. A fallback nobody renders is a fallback
            nobody proofreads. */}
        Between releases — build it from source with <code class="font-mono">make app</code>.
      </p>
    )
  }
</section>
